    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0393" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg309"/>

                <head>No. 149.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pendleton to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 16, 1885</date>.
                        (Received November 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 110.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I send herewith report and translation of a
                    speech made by Count Kalnoky, the Austrian premier, in the Austrian Chamber, as
                    the report appears in the Nord Preussische Zeitung of this city, and another
                    report on the same speech taken from the London Times.</p>
                <p>Count Kalnoky admits as beyond controversy the right of Germany under the laws of
                    nations to refuse sojourn to foreigners with or without cause according to its
                    own will, and this under a very stringent exercise of that right against
                    Austrian subjects.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. H. PENDLETON.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d153-a1.xml" xpointer="d153-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d153-a2.xml" xpointer="d153-a2"/>
